nt": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01B1qLefr5TV8RHfDmTQWhMT", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 2, "runtime_actions": ["backoff_retry", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 378764, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01B1qLefr5TV8RHfDmTQWhMT", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383119, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py` was failing.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** #101 (https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). I haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n\nI couldn't check FIN-212 itself because the advisory tool didn't recognise that ID. The fix is based on what the test and the docstring expect.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Q8LiEDzZ8PpxKX2Vp4Fhm4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_014pUXmfhgCATp287536owBX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01YQk3XxkXQ1txF3CSuvrdPp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content":